<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fujiwara no Sumitomo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 941</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fujiwara no Sumitomo was a Japanese court noble and warrior of the Heian era who led a revolt in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 939 to 941. Having built a power base in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> and made a secret agreement with Taira no Masakado, who was in revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimosa-province">Shimōsa Province</a>, he rose in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iyo-province">Iyo Province</a> in 939 and invaded Harima and Bizen, and the revolt spread through the whole <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanyo-region">San'yō region</a>. Pursued by imperial forces under Ono no Yoshifuru and Minamoto no Tsunemoto, he fled to Dazaifu and burned its headquarters before being defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakata">Hakata</a> Bay. He was captured in Iyo and executed in 941 by Tachibana no Tōyasu. He was the ancestor of the Arima clan of Hizen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fujiwara-no-sumitomo.jpg" alt="Fujiwara no Sumitomo" width="303" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fujiwara_no_Sumitomo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Gradually the provincial upper class became a new military elite of samurai, who helped suppress the risings in Hitachi in the east and of <b>Fujiwara no Sumitomo</b> in the west; final authority still rested with the court.</blockquote><a href="/societies/heian-japan">Social Hierarchy of Heian Japan</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iyo-province">Iyo Province</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=33.74,132.91&amp;year=931" aria-label="Iyo Province on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7941 940 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Fujiwara no Sumitomo"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8391 1210h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8391 1210h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=33.74,132.91&amp;year=931">What was here in 931 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
